{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3811"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Collection of non-hazardous waste"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3811"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :utilities/non-hazardous-waste-collection
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:environmental-protection :public-health :operational-transparency]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :waste-dispatch-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "WasteDispatch-LLM (sealed advisor) ⊣ WasteDispatchGovernor (independent
  censor), a genuinely compiled langgraph-clj StateGraph
  (wastecollect.operation/build: :intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide
  -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold, with
  `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + checkpointer for real
  human-in-the-loop resume). Eight governor checks (wastecollect.policy)
  gate every schedule/record/disclosure/dispute: rbac,
  hazard-misclassification-gate and facility-permit-capacity-gate
  (domain-unique HARD checks — no analog in sibling actors),
  source-provenance-gate, licensed-disclosure, confidence floor,
  bulk-volume gate, dispute-request-always-escalates. Schedules pickups,
  records collection manifests and serves client reports for
  non-hazardous waste generators/facilities only — a pickup carrying ANY
  hazard flag is structurally rejected by the
  hazard-misclassification-gate at any confidence, regardless of phase;
  no field anywhere in the schema exists for hazardous-waste handling,
  storage or transport (ADR-2607113200 §1). Real regulatory-provenance
  catalog (wastecollect.facts): US RCRA, EU Waste Framework Directive,
  Japan's 廃棄物処理法 — every classification claim must cite one of these,
  none fabricated. Append-only audit ledger (wastecollect.store/ledger +
  append-ledger!), Store protocol with MemStore (default) and
  DatomicStore (langchain.db) backends proven to the same contract
  (store_contract_test.clj); DatomicStore's EDN-blob codec uses
  kotoba-lang/langchain-store's shared `ls/enc` / `ls/dec*` rather than a
  bespoke pr-str/edn-read-string pair. Phase 0->3 staged-autonomy gate
  (wastecollect.phase), conservative default-phase=1 from initial
  implementation, that can only narrow — never widen — what the governor
  already allows. 33 tests / 126 assertions green
  (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors/warnings
  (`clojure -M:lint`), demo runnable end-to-end (`clojure -M:dev:run`,
  8-operation walkthrough through one OperationActor). Deliberately
  distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-3822 (treatment/disposal of hazardous
  waste): this actor dispatches non-hazardous streams only, 3822 treats/
  disposes hazardous waste under RCRA Subtitle C / the EU Waste Shipment
  Regulation / the Basel Convention."}
